This product includes no ROMs, game scripts or JMdict data.

yomineko downloads JMdict at runtime (`yomineko dict download`) and does not ship it.
JMdict is the property of the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group (EDRDG)
and is used under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence:
https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html

The word analysis uses SudachiPy and SudachiDict-core (Works Applications, Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/WorksApplications/Sudachi). The pip package installs them as separate
dependencies; the desktop builds include them, and each library's own licence file is kept in
the bundle. SudachiDict is built from UniDic and other sources: see
https://github.com/WorksApplications/SudachiDict for its terms.

The JMdict download trusts the certificates in certifi (https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi,
Mozilla Public License 2.0), which the pip package installs as a dependency and the desktop builds
include unmodified.

The web interface includes two files from other projects, unmodified:
- htmx 2.0.4 (https://htmx.org), Zero-Clause BSD licence.
- Pico CSS 2.0.6 (https://picocss.com), Copyright (c) 2019-2024 Pico, MIT licence.

The web interface bundles six font files, unmodified, in src/yomineko/web/static/fonts/: IBM Plex
Sans 1.1.0, IBM Plex Sans JP 3.0.0 and IBM Plex Mono 2.5.0 (https://github.com/IBM/plex), each in
Regular and SemiBold. Copyright 2017 IBM Corp. with Reserved Font Name "Plex", licensed under the SIL
Open Font License, Version 1.1 (https://openfontlicense.org). The full licence text is next to the
fonts, in OFL.txt, and goes with them in the package and the desktop builds.

The logo (docs/assets/logo.png) is an illustration by @loritoart. It is not covered by the
Apache-2.0 licence of the code.
